Man: I grab a burger and fries with a large soft drink almost every day.
Woman: That''s a lot of sugar and fat. Maybe you should try grilled chicken with salad instead.
Man: But I love fast food. Doesn''t the protein in a burger help?
Woman: Some, but the extra sugar and salt outweigh the benefit. Try to add one salad a week and drink more water.
Man: Okay, I''ll start with the salad every Thursday and see how I feel.', 'Why does the woman say the burger is not a good choice?', '[{"id":"a","text":"Because the restaurant is too far from his office"},{"id":"b","text":"Because burgers are too expensive for every day"},{"id":"c","text":"Because the extra sugar and salt outweigh the benefit"},{"id":"d","text":"Because the man is allergic to some kinds of meat"}]'::jsonb, 'c', 'The woman says the protein helps a little, "but the extra sugar and salt outweigh the benefit."', 'medium', array['listening-comprehension']::text[]) on conflict (id) do update set section = excluded.section, course_id = excluded.course_id, passage_id = excluded.passage_id, audio_url = excluded.audio_url, transcript = excluded.transcript, prompt = excluded.prompt, options = excluded.options, correct_option_id = excluded.correct_option_id, explanation = excluded.explanation, difficulty = excluded.difficulty, tags = excluded.tags;
insert into public.questions (id, section, course_id, passage_id, audio_url, transcript, prompt, options, correct_option_id, explanation, difficulty, tags) values ('q-listening-68', 'listening', null, null, '/audio/listening/q-listening-66.mp3', 'Woman: You always seem tired after lunch. What do you usually eat?
Man: I grab a burger and fries with a large soft drink almost every day.
Woman: That''s a lot of sugar and fat. Maybe you should try grilled chicken with salad instead.
Man: But I love fast food. Doesn''t the protein in a burger help?
Woman: Some, but the extra sugar and salt outweigh the benefit. Try to add one salad a week and drink more water.
Man: Okay, I''ll start with the salad every Thursday and see how I feel.', 'What will the man most likely do after this conversation?', '[{"id":"a","text":"Stop eating fast food completely from tomorrow"},{"id":"b","text":"Give up soft drinks entirely and drink only juice"},{"id":"c","text":"Order grilled chicken every day for lunch"},{"id":"d","text":"Eat a salad every Thursday and drink more water"}]'::jsonb, 'd', 'The man agrees to "start with the salad every Thursday and see how I feel."', 'medium', array['listening-inference']::text[]) on conflict (id) do update set section = excluded.section, course_id = excluded.course_id, passage_id = excluded.passage_id, audio_url = excluded.audio_url, transcript = excluded.transcript, prompt = excluded.prompt, options = excluded.options, correct_option_id = excluded.correct_option_id, explanation = excluded.explanation, difficulty = excluded.difficulty, tags = excluded.tags;
insert into public.questions (id, section, course_id, passage_id, audio_url, transcript, prompt, options, correct_option_id, explanation, difficulty, tags) values ('q-listening-69', 'listening', null, null, '/audio/listening/q-listening-69.mp3', 'Student: Doctor, every winter I feel exhausted and I want to sleep all day.
Doctor: How long has this been happening?
Student: It started about three years ago, always around November and December.
Doctor: This pattern sounds like seasonal affective disorder, or SAD. Many patients feel much better when they get more morning sunlight.
Student: I usually stay indoors all day, so would a special lamp help?
Doctor: Yes, light therapy works well, and so does a short walk outside. I suggest the morning walk first, then a lamp if you still need it.', 'Around which months do the student''s symptoms usually appear?', '[{"id":"a","text":"January and February"},{"id":"b","text":"November and December"},{"id":"c","text":"June and July"},{"id":"d","text":"All year long"}]'::jsonb, 'b', 'The student says the problem "started about three years ago, always around November and December."', 'easy', array['listening-comprehension']::text[]) on conflict (id) do update set section = excluded.section, course_id = excluded.course_id, passage_id = excluded.passage_id, audio_url = excluded.audio_url, transcript = excluded.transcript, prompt = excluded.prompt, options = excluded.options, correct_option_id = excluded.correct_option_id, explanation = excluded.explanation, difficulty = excluded.difficulty, tags = excluded.tags;
